=== Major regions ===

The largest region, Lower-central central savanna (region 1), covers 439,306 km² of the central and south-western interior at a mean elevation of roughly 300 m. It is the driest major region of Sinchew, receiving 1,420 mm annually, and is classified predominantly as tropical savanna with humid subtropical conditions in its southern portions. Its relative dryness reflects its distance from the eastern moisture source and its position leeward of the highlands.

Lower-central east humid lowlands (region 2) lies between the savanna interior and the eastern highlands, receiving 2,010 mm and supporting a mixture of humid subtropical, savanna and monsoon conditions. Its higher rainfall relative to the savanna region to its west reflects its greater proximity to the windward slopes.

The Upper-central east monsoon belt (regions 3 and 5) comprises two adjacent areas of 206,399 and 150,074 km² respectively, both strongly dominated by tropical monsoon conditions with precipitation of 3,460 and 3,476 mm. These regions lie east of centre and at moderate elevation.

Upper-central west monsoon belt (region 4) covers 157,453 km² of the interior and is transitional, receiving 1,943 mm and splitting almost evenly between monsoon and savanna types. The contrast with its eastern counterpart illustrates the strength of the orographic gradient.

Upper-central central rainforest (region 6) and Upper-central east rainforest (region 8) together span some 243,000 km² in the upper-central latitudes, receiving 3,277 and 4,533 mm respectively and classified principally as tropical rainforest. Northern central rainforest (region 11) is the wettest major region by precipitation, at 4,812 mm, and the warmest, with a mean annual temperature of 26.6 °C.

=== Highland regions ===

Four regions are classified principally as subtropical highland and owe their character to elevation rather than latitude. Lower-central Highland (region 10) is the largest, covering 74,490 km² at a mean elevation of 1,682 m, with a mean annual temperature of 12.9 °C and precipitation of 4,206 mm. Lower-central Highland II (region 16), Southern Highland (region 19) and Southern Highland II (region 23) are progressively smaller and lower, with temperatures between 15.2 and 17.0 °C.

These regions form the only part of Sinchew in which mean annual temperatures fall below 18 °C, and they constitute the country's principal climatic anomaly: although they lie at latitudes that elsewhere support tropical rainforest or savanna, their elevation produces conditions more typical of the subtropics.

=== Minor and local regions ===

The remaining regions are smaller in extent but climatically distinct. Lower-central west monsoon belt (region 7) is unusual in combining a high mean annual temperature of 24.7 °C with an elevation near sea level and 2,418 mm of rainfall. Lower-central west savanna (regions 12 and 15) covers the driest parts of the country, with 1,266 and 1,728 mm respectively and predominant savanna classification.

Upper-central west monsoon belt II through V (regions 13, 14, 20 and 21) are small areas of the western interior exhibiting a range of conditions from 1,935 to 4,498 mm, the latter reflecting a locally favourable exposure to moist flow. Upper-central east rainforest II (region 22) and Upper-central central monsoon belt (region 17) are comparably small but characteristic of their respective zones.

== Extremes ==

The wettest parts of Sinchew are the windward slopes of the eastern highlands, where annual totals exceed 5,700 mm, among the highest recorded anywhere in the country. The driest is the western interior, with a minimum of 795 mm. The highest mean annual temperature, 27.0 °C, occurs in the northern lowlands; the lowest, 5.3 °C, occurs on the highest summits above 2,400 m, which are the only parts of Sinchew to experience regular frost.

